  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training how to export food products to the EU, especially the Netherlands</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lebanon experienced the worst economic and financial crisis in its modern history. Since late 2019, private banks have imposed informal capital controls, limiting withdrawals and halting transfers abroad. Meanwhile, the value of the Lebanese currency fell against the dollar amid an unprecedented shortage of foreign currencies, leading to a sharp increase in poverty and unemployment. The scarcity of foreign currency in the country necessitates companies to increase exports to stay afloat and halt the effects of inflation and local currency depreciation. This project will help Lebanese Small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) increase their potential for export by increasing their understanding of rules, regulations and requirements to export to the European market.</narrative>
  </description>
